    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nIf a window is split and afterwards the window is resized, the split position won't be updated regarding to the new dimensions. \n\nExample: \nThe window has a width of 1000 pixels. The user splits the pane, the left pane will be 500 pixels and the right pane will be 500 pixels. After resizing the window to be 2000 pixels, left will be 500 pixels and right 1500 pixels.  \n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open terminal \n2. Split pane \n3. Resize terminal window\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe split should be based on percentages, and automatically recalculated. So for a window that is 2000 pixels after resizing and currently split by 50% it will still do 1000 pixels left and right.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.12.4\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nYes\n\n### Operating system/version\n\n7.1.5-arch1-2\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nghostty version=1.3.1-arch2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nghostty\n\n### Installation\n\npacman",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
