        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "One thing to take into consideration here is that what if user *doesn't want* to have windows automatically resize on `VimResized`? Like if some window is deliberately set to have a dimension *exactly* `n` number of cells, maybe this makes the presentation look better and occupy just enough space. Like some kind of tree viewer at the left or symbol outline at the right.\n\nIf all windows are automatically resized on `VimResized`, then it is much more effort for these kind of use cases to be implemented than what is currently needed to make windows auto-equalize.\n\n> So for a window that is 2000 pixels after resizing and currently split by 50% it will still do 1000 pixels left and right.\n\nThe main problem here is that there is no notion of \"window width is set to be 50% of total width\". There is only \"window width is set to be `n` cells\". The described behavior would be reasonable in case fractional window widths are supported to mean this kind of percentage. Otherwise I think the current behavior is much less surprising and problematic to deal with; while also being one short one-liner away from making it auto-equalize.",
            "created_at": "2026-07-30T17:26:42Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41059#issuecomment-5134125647",
            "id": 5134125647,
