        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "An argument in favor of the current Vim/Nvim behavior: it lets you *temporarily* resize the container terminal/GUI without messing up your window layout. (However, it could be interesting to automatically restore window layouts at specific dimensions.)\n\n> what if user _doesn't want_ to have windows automatically resize on `VimResized`? \n\nIf (if) we decide to make this a default, the user would just delete the default `VimResized` handler in the `nvim.x` augroup.\n\n> Like if some window is deliberately set to have a dimension _exactly_ `n` number of cells\n\n`:wincmd =` respects 'winfixheight' / 'winfixwidth', I think that addresses that?",
            "created_at": "2026-07-30T19:05:01Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41059#issuecomment-5135117577",
            "id": 5135117577,
            "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/41059",
            "minimized": null,
            "node_id": "IC_kwDOAPphoM8AAAABMhOtCQ",
            "performed_via_github_app": null,
            "pin": null,
